面的大夫人看着不住的点头。若柳蓉知道大夫人心中的评价，肯定会哭笑不得，她不过是行现代人尊老爱幼的美德罢了，至于不争宠，这样偏心的老人面前，她争个啥劲？却说太夫人年纪毕竟大了，闲时最大的爱好便是含饴弄孙，这也是柳璇会被宠的不知天高地厚，不顾侯府安危，非要太夫人找人替换她入宫的原因。如今听到玄孙和孙媳妇有危险，如何不急，脚下的步子明明不稳当，迈开的步子却丝毫不停顿。一时之间，刘大奶奶和柳璇竟有些扶不住太夫人，一旁看着担忧的大夫人赶忙上前替了柳璇。柳蓉想了想，靠近几步：“太祖母您还是慢些，您这般着急，若是不小心磕着了，到时候二奶奶那边危急，祖母和二祖母还有母亲可就没了主心骨了。”柳蓉说着话，心里却是鄙视自己，明明是想说对方这会生病会耽误事，不过想到李妈妈毕竟对自己不错，能帮二奶奶那边减少点麻烦，是一点。太夫人虽然没有回答，步子却慢了一些，刘大奶奶和大夫人瞬间轻松许多。只是刘大奶奶虽然轻松了，望着柳蓉的脸色却不好看。大夫人则对着柳蓉笑着点头。之后才继续扶着太夫人前行。柳蓉微微一愣，刘大奶奶的反应是预料之中，大夫人的反应却叫她有些奇怪，不过想不通的事情，她从不为难自己多想，不然人生在世，总是这么逼着自己多累。大约也是因为这一点，上一世才会选择做个外科大夫，做个只动刀子即可的医生吧。跟着一行人出了屋子，太夫人的排场果然不一样，这一出院子，丫鬟婆子的竟有二十多人，却是浩浩荡荡的开向梨园。快速走过长廊，到得假山拐弯之处，突然迎面冲来一个一身亮色袄子，头发高高挽起的中年妇人，只见她脚步快速，见到他们竟一时间刹不住，两行人差点没冲撞上。看清对方相貌，太夫人眉头皱起：“慌什么，二奶奶那边虽然危急，但也不差这一时半会，万一你这二房主事的出了事情，到时候二奶奶谁管。”赶的匆忙之人竟是二奶奶的婆婆，这侯府的二夫人。二夫人被当着大家的面训斥，面色有些不好：“母亲说的是，只是我家二爷续的媳妇，身子也不知是怎么娇惯的，平时也不好好照顾自己，竟在府中宴请人时突然出了这样的事情，我也实在着急，怕耽搁事，才会这般慌的乱了手脚。”一段话说的直教人蹙眉，二夫人却丝毫不觉着自己有问题，仅仅微微一顿，便面带讨好的走到太夫人身旁：“母亲，我扶您一起去梨园吧。”刘大奶奶乖巧适时的退后，将自己的位置让给二夫人，二夫人对着刘大奶奶满意的点头，明显喜欢。如此一折腾，这一路便花了一盏茶的时间。待到得梨园，只见产房外丫鬟婆子冲冲忙忙来回跑着，而一个一身锦袍，明显是这屋子男主人的中年人却是面上毫无担心的训斥着一个年龄略比柳蓉大一些的少年。“你母亲如今正是危急，你怎还有心呼朋唤友，你是要让所有人都知道侯府二少爷不知孝道吗？”“父亲……”太夫人看到这一幕，脚步更急，脸色也不好，一旁路上遇到的二夫人面色铁青，松开太夫人的手快步上前：“这是怎么回事，不是说二奶奶危急了吗，怎么还在这里教训孩子？御医可请来了，稳婆怎么说？”“祖母！祖母！继母就是那么回事，重要的是太子世子今日来了府里，我……我一时有事……太子世子便不见了……”还不等二爷开口，一旁的少年急忙上前开口，面上越说越急：“您快叫人帮我找找吧，万一世子不见了，祖母，这可如何是好。”二夫人一听，先是一急，继而眼睛一亮，面上却不动声色的对着身旁的人吩咐：“杜妈妈，你在这里看着，其它人，都赶紧领着人去找太子世子，无论在什么地方一定要找出来。”“博哥儿，你跟我走，告诉我具体究竟是发生了什么事情？你又是怎么和太子世子交好上的，若是弄的好，说不定这件事情对你父亲的仕途大有益处。”说着话，二夫人露出一个大大的笑容，竟是急的连同太夫人打个招呼的心情都没有，便直接领着柳博离开，完全不管产房中难产的二奶奶的死活。太夫人面色铁青，大夫人赶忙给太夫人顺了顺气，才自己上前询问二爷：“稳婆怎么说？御医可曾看了？”“御医刚刚进去，只是稳婆说丹青头一胎胎位不正，孩子在里面出不来。如今羊水已经破了好些时候，说是不快些生下来，恐怕会不好。”二爷对着大夫人恭敬的说道，只是眼睛却是时不时的跟着自己母亲和自己的长子，如此虽然回答的详细，却明显心不在焉。柳蓉一旁看得直皱眉，她听钟氏说过，二奶奶是个温厚的人，对她们也不错，有时候甚至会救济她们，对李妈妈也熟悉，所以才会出了事情厚脸皮来梨园。如今见这个男人在二奶奶难产之时，不仅没有担心，竟更关心自己儿子和太子世子的相处之事，柳蓉便忍不住一阵厌恶，也为二奶奶心疼。“御医出来了。”不知是谁喊了那么一句，太夫人和大夫人一行人便向产房前靠近，只见一个一身朝服的御医面无表情的走出。“史御医，我家玄孙子怎么样了？可能顺利产下来？”太夫人望着御医快速的问道。史御医见到太夫人，表情略微沉重：“二奶奶如今气虚不通，怕是很难。”“不保大人，只保孩子都不行吗？”太夫人继续追问道。柳蓉直听得眉头更紧，忍不住转头看向一旁跟着出来的李妈妈，只见对方面色惨白，叫人看了万分不忍。“这……”御医为难。“求求你，你一定要救救二奶奶，一定要救救二奶奶啊！”李妈妈似乎被什么激的突然清醒过来一般，快速上前，对着史御医跪下恳求。“不是我不帮忙，我是真的无能为力，孩子根本生不下来，那催产的药物也已经给二奶奶服下了，你也看到了，根本没有效果。”李妈妈一呆滑坐在地上。她是二奶奶从娘家带来的妈妈，感情本就深厚，除此之外，却还有一层旁人不知道的关系，那便是她是二奶奶的乳娘，是奶着二奶奶长大的，二奶奶之余她便如亲生女儿一般。听到自己视为亲生女儿的二奶奶就要没了，她只觉得天旋地转。柳蓉赶忙上前扶住李妈妈，掐了一下她大拇指和食指之间的穴位，待见李妈妈稍微好些才松手。“我的玄孙啊！”听了史御医的话，太夫人忍不住哀嚎，刘大奶奶和柳璇赶忙上前劝说。“太夫人可要保重身体。”史御医也跟着一旁劝解着。李妈妈一片茫然，忍不住握住柳蓉的手：“二奶奶，我的二奶奶，真的就不行了吗？就要没了吗？”柳蓉心底一颤，望着李妈妈的意识不清的面庞，想到之前求药，李妈妈不仅将药给了自己，还叫人给自己拿补药，不禁心底一软，伸手反握李妈妈：“怎么会，不到最后，都还有机会！”“哪有什么机会，御医都说不行了！”说着，李妈妈竟是痛哭起来。柳蓉眉头一皱，一咬牙，像是做了什么决定一般站起身，迈步走向产房。", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/houmenyinu/4.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 4 Liu Rong, a top member of the family, lowered her head to prevent others from seeing her expression. Even to her, a time traveler, the words of the madam were no longer just angry, but felt harsh and sad for her body. To be reincarnated into such a family. But these people wanted to force this thing on her, couldn't she ruin it? Thinking of this, Liu Rong looked up expressionlessly. \"My wife is not good, something serious is going wrong, my second grandma... my second grandma is having a difficult delivery, I'm afraid she may die!\" Liu Rong was about to speak, when suddenly the maid's alarm came from far away, she was slightly startled and did not continue. \"Why are you panicking? You are the maid of the Hou Mansion! Don't be so panicked when anything happens! You are so reckless. Regardless of whether the news is conveyed well or not, what should I do if the wife is shocked?\" Then the voice of Mother Chen outside the door scolded: \"Don't go out to receive the punishment yourself.\" \"Yes...\" There was a weak response from outside, and the silence returned. But Mother Chen trotted in with small steps. The madam, who was feeling sorry for Liu Xuan and gently stroking Liu Xuan's hair to comfort her, changed her expression. Before Mother Chen could speak, she stood up quickly. She sat back down because she was too hasty, and when she thought about it again, she couldn't hold herself up. Liu Xuan, who was kneeling beside him, was stunned and didn't know what to do. Liu Rong, who was standing closest and could see clearly, frowned. Although she didn't like it in her heart, the person in front of her who couldn't get up was an old man after all. In the end, she quickly stepped forward and helped the lady up. \"What's going on? Why did something like this happen? Come on, come on, let's go and have a look.\" Madam Tai stood up with strength, but didn't even look at Liu Rong. Liu Rong touched her nose and stood aside silently. The madam's hand did not let go of her arm, and she continued to stand with her strength. However, in this moment of impatience, even though the Madam was older, her hands were quite strong and she pulled her arm hard until it hurt. Liu Xuan on the side finally reacted and hurriedly stepped forward to hold Mrs. Tai's other arm. Grandma Liu, who had already stepped forward, stepped forward and pushed her aside. Seeing someone rushing to do the hard work, Liu Rongle felt relaxed and quickly stepped aside. Not arrogant, not impetuous, not fighting for favor, Mr. Zhong’s teaching is good, and the girl is not bad either. The eldest lady who followed could not help but nodded. If Liu Rong knew what the eldest lady was thinking, she would definitely be dumbfounded. She was just practicing the modern virtue of respecting the old and loving the young. As for not competing for favor, how could she fight in front of such a partial old man? However, she said that Mrs. Tai was old after all, and her biggest hobby in her spare time was to entertain her grandchildren. This was why Liu Xuanhui was so favored that she ignored the safety of the Hou Mansion and insisted on finding someone to replace her in the palace. Now that I heard that my great-great-grandson and granddaughter-in-law were in danger, I was not in a hurry. The steps under my feet were obviously unsteady, but my steps did not stop at all. For a moment, Grandma Liu and Liu Xuan were unable to support the madam. The worried madam looked on and hurriedly stepped forward to replace Liu Xuan. Liu Rong thought for a while and took a few steps closer: \"Great-grandmother, please slow down. If you are in such a hurry, if you accidentally knock yourself, the second grandma will be in danger, and the grandmother, second grandmother, and mother will have no backbone.\" Liu Rong said, but she despised herself in her heart. She obviously wanted to say that the other party would get sick and delay things, but she thought that Mother Li was kind to her after all, and could help the second grandma reduce some trouble. Although Mrs. Tai did not answer, her steps were slower. Grandma Liu and Mrs. Liu felt much more relaxed instantly. It's just that although Grandma Liu was relaxed, her expression when she looked at Liu Rong was not good-looking. The eldest lady smiled and nodded at Liu Rong. Then he continued to help the madam move forward. Liu Rong was slightly startled. Grandma Liu's reaction was expected, but the reaction of the eldest lady made her a little strange. However, she never made it difficult for her to think too much about things that she couldn't figure out, otherwise she would always be so tired in her life. Probably because of this, I chose to be a surgeon in my last life, a doctor who could only use the knife. After following the group of people out of the house, the pomp of the wife was indeed different. When they came out of the yard, there were more than twenty maids and women, but they drove towards the opera garden in a mighty manner. I walked quickly through the corridor and reached the corner of the rockery. Suddenly, a middle-aged woman wearing a bright-colored jacket and her hair tied high rushed towards me. She was walking very fast. When she saw them, she couldn't stop for a moment, and the two groups almost collided with each other. Seeing the other party's appearance clearly, the Madam frowned: \"Why are you panicking? Although the Second Grandma is in danger, it won't last long. If something happens to you, the second house owner, who will take care of it then?\" The person who was in a hurry was actually the Second Grandma's mother-in-law, the second lady of the Hou Mansion. The second wife was reprimanded in front of everyone, and her face looked a little bad: \"What mother said is that she is just the daughter-in-law of my second master. I don't know how she is pampered, and she doesn't take good care of herself. Suddenly, something like this happened when we were having a banquet in the house. I was really anxious, and I was afraid of delaying things, so I was so panicked.\" The direct teacher frowned at what he said, but the second lady didn't realize that there was anything wrong with her. After just a slight pause, she walked to the madam with a flattering expression: \"Mother, let me help you go to the opera garden with you.\" Grandma Liu stepped back obediently and in time, and gave up her position to the second lady. The second lady nodded with satisfaction at Grandma Liu, obviously liking her. After all this trouble, it took a cup of tea. When they arrived at the Liyuan, they saw maids and women running back and forth in a hurry outside the delivery room, while a middle-aged man in a brocade robe, who was obviously the master of the house, scolded a young man who was slightly older than Liu Rong without any worry on his face. \"Your mother is in critical condition right now. How can you still have the heart to call out your friends? Do you want everyone to know that the second young master of the Hou Mansion does not know filial piety?\" \"Father...\" Mrs. Tai raised her feet when she saw this scene.", "translated": true, "title_en": "Chapter 4"}